# Google sign-in for Gurukul Studio (the desktop app): the "Desktop app" OAuth client in the
# nonstop-gurukul Google Cloud project (Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials).
#
# Build-time configuration, written into dist/main.cjs by scripts/bundle.ts. Copy this file to
# apps/desktop/.env (gitignored) for `npm run dev -w @gurukul/desktop`, or export the variables;
# a variable already set wins over the file. The release build reads both from GitHub Actions
# secrets of the same names. Left empty, the app opens but "Sign in with Google" says this build
# cannot sign in.
#
# Google does not treat a Desktop client's secret as confidential (it ships inside every installer),
# but this repository is public: never commit either value (.plan/13-open-questions.md, question 22).
GURUKUL_DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GURUKUL_DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
